{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat collab/1792770000000-architect-8c-ruling-and-review.report.md; sed -n '448,485p' test/yin/vm/linker_manifest_test.cljc; rg -n 'other-program|worked-example' test/yin/vm/linker_test.cljc; head -10 collab/1792780000000-engineer-8c-fix1.codex.stdout.log\"","aggregated_output":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-14 21:35 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-15 04:35 +07\nCoding-Agent: claude (claude-fable-5-1), Architect\nSession-ID: 9cb6b611-09f3-427d-8ce2-093a958097df\n# Architect: 8c ruling and review of the uncommitted srvm-phase8c diff (base 30d4c72c)\n\nScope: `git diff` (29 files, byte-identical to `collab/8c-uncommitted.diff` before and after my mutants; `diff` exit 0 at the end), the codex report, brief, plan, my previous sign-off, derivations §7.6/§8.3, linker.md §3 amendment, codex's logs under `target/8c/`. Everything below was rerun by me on the JVM unless marked \"codex's\".\n\n## What I verified\n| Suite (JVM, foreground) | Result |\n|---|---|\n| publish, linker-manifest, closure, ledger, serve, link, production-pipeline, ucf, code tests | 121 tests, 927 assertions, **1 failure** (F1) |\n| linker-test, linker-require-test | 107 tests, 1741 assertions, 0 failures |\n| derive-test, rows-test (20 A pins), remote-transfer-test | 63 tests, 6995 assertions, 0 failures |\n| cross-host-transfer-test (JVM + freshly built Dart peer, unmutated source) | 1 test, 24 assertions, 0 failures (seen on the M-B run's control: the non-forged legs pass) |\n| yang.python linked-prelude + linked-safepoint (regenerated pins) | 27 tests, 173 assertions, 8 failures, 2 errors: exactly the semantic leg (`semantic.cljc:797` arity defect, `engine.cljc:52`); the py/pysp manifest-golden deftests PASS, so the two pins are correct |\n| scan-test | not finished by me (killed at the 20 min limit); codex's identity gate log covers it |\nA gates: `corpus.cljc`, `rows_test.cljc`, `derive_test.cljc`, `debruijn_code_test.cljc`, `debruijn_register_code_test.cljc` have no diff. `rows-checkpoint-v3.txt`: 5 hunks, all inside the `installs` block and the two `child-*` lines, as reported. Only the two authorized `test/yang/` files changed. Remaining requirers: my grep equals the report's ten lines exactly; old-kernel requirers are the two demos and the Dart bench (8f). `yin.vm.completion` is required only by `ucf/handoff.cljc:59` (Q5 evidence holds). kondo and the Node REPL build are codex's (0 warnings, 226 files); I did not rerun Node or Dart lanes.\n\n## Mutants (mine; cp backup, test, restore, diff vs snapshot identical each time)\n| Mutant | Killed by |\n|---|---|\n| M-A closure walk compares native record input to the tree again | closure-test, 10 deftests |\n| M-C checked-derivation skips the nested semantic leg (expected := record's own input) | linker-manifest-test `native-verification-checks-the-semantic-derivation-too` |\n| M-D relowered returns R for the stack format | linker-manifest-test, 5 deftests |\n| M-B link-local identity-matches-fn drops the checksum (keeps only `(= A a)`) | **survives** publish, manifest, require, dht, closure (110 tests green); killed only by the JVM+Dart cross-host test, and there the foreign bytes passed step 3 and were stopped at the obligation join (`:undeclared-free`), not by `:hash-mismatch` |\n\n## Findings\n| id | sev | file:line | finding | fix |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| F1 | P2 | test/yin/vm/semantic_register/link_test.cljc:132 | `(assoc marker :yin.k/format :yin.semantic/code)` is a no-op after the keyword move, so the `:binding-mismatch` assertion fails on the unmutated tree; this suite is in the 8c acceptance list and the report calls it green (its mutant log shows 4 failures, one of them this baseline) | use a foreign format, e.g. `:yin.debruijn.code` |\n| F2 | P2 | src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:2289 | the native checksum check of the manifest path has no JVM test (M-B); the one killer is cross-host and kills it by accident of the fixture's free name | one linker-manifest-test deftest: publish two modules, point module 1's index entry for each native format at module 2's image address, `link-manifest` must refuse `:hash-mismatch` under both policies |\n| F3 | P3 | src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc:152 | refusal evidence `:expected` is the tree for native records although the check compares against A | report the compared value |\n| F4 | P3 | src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:2189, :2297 | a `:verifying` semantic request fetches A and runs `verify-derivation` twice (verified-policy-outcome, then linked-image); correct, redundant | skip the second when `:tree` is present and the first ran; may wait for 8f |\n| F5 | P3 ledger | src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:744, linearize.cljc:474 | the old kernel and old lowerer now stamp and accept `\"v4\"` through `vm/semantic-contract` on v3-shaped vectors; no producer, dies in 8f; it is why the harness fails with an arity defect, not `:contract-mismatch` | ledger entry; 8f deletes both |\n| F6 | P3 ledger | src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:656-690, :951-960; test/yin/vm/linker/remote_transfer_test.cljc:197 | by-identity native `fetch`/`publish!`/`index-from-datoms` still name native bytes by H/R; linker.md §3 amendment retires H/R as names, and no `source-index` (A to trees) exists anywhere in `src/`; outside the 8c row | 8e/8f item plus the linker.md §4-§8 rewrite the amendment promises |\n| F7 | P3 | src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf.cljc:47 | `:yin.k/version` 0 to 1 is beyond the brief's text but is plan §1.5 (\"contract-stamp becomes the rows profile\"); `ledger/lowering-profile` stays version 0 (a different profile) | none; recorded |\n| F8 | P3 | test/yin/vm/semantic_register/scan_test.cljc | `print-goldens` deleted (fixture now unregenerable, acceptable: pinned history) while `old-linearize` is still required for one comparison | 8f |\n\n## Review answers\n(1) Invariants hold on the manifest path: records are `tree -> A`, `A -> H`, `A -> R`; index `{format storage-address}`; native `:identities` return A, H/R under `:checksums`; the stepped fetch requests native bytes by A with a link-local `{A addr}` index and a link-local matches-fn (A equality plus checksum), state discarded after the link (`link-manifest` drops it), so nothing leaks into the composition. This is derivations §7.6 and the linker.md amendment (\"a request names {:format f :hash A}; the index maps [A f]\") made code. The nested semantic leg under both policies means a forged semantic record cannot rename native bytes (M-C). Tree kept in the manifest and materialized; BLAKE3 untouched; no kernel or lowerer deleted; keyword moved once (grep: only docs mention the old one); refusing old index keys at admission is a legitimate clean break under the no-compat rule. Gap: F6.\n(2) Q5: agree. Completion has no live v4 caller; a projection would be a second implementation serving the retired codec only.\n(3) A gate: byte-identical as listed above; pins confirmed by the passing golden deftests.\n(4) Dart transfer peer: sound. It links over the manifest with the six format records and the default `:verifying` policy, so the Dart side runs the whole chain (tree, semantic record, A, tree -> A, relowering, checksum). Cosmetic: the hash-mismatch evidence now pairs an A under `:expected` with an H under `:actual`.\n(5) Codex's six mutants are plausible; my four add M-B, which exposes the F2 gap.\n(6) vm.cljc: `semantic-bytecode-child-refs` had zero references; the three renames are `_`-prefixes of unused locals. No behaviour change.\n(7) Inventory complete and exactly the 8e/8f set.\n(8) Node/Dart: `(assoc {} ...)`, no long `for`, portable catches, no private access; the new `production_pipeline_test` is JVM-only by design (slurps paths). Orchestrator still owes Node (`bb test:changed` cljs) and Dart lanes on the final tree.\n\n## RULING: C\nLand 8c and the harness port together as one slice (`8c+harness`) on `srvm-phase8c`, under a freeze on exactly one more C4 file: `test/yang/python/antlr/linked_harness.cljc` (the two pin files are already under the 8ab precedent). Reasons: A is refused because `srvm-phase8` is 8e's base and 8e edits the ten C4 files anyway, so the freeze is unavoidable before 8e; a red yang.python shard on the integration branch for the weeks of 8e would mask regressions in the one suite that is the phase's proof, and \"carving out\" a shard means an allowlist nobody owns. B is the same content but would move the diff I reviewed; C keeps this diff frozen and makes the port a separate, mechanically reviewable commit. D is a shim: two live producers of one semantic identity for the same code; I rule it forbidden. The port is six sites in `linked_harness.cljc:105-140` (`semantic-loader`, the three `backends` lambdas, the two `continues` lambdas): `:semantic` becomes `semantic-register/create-vm` plus `load-vector` over `(:vector (sr-linearize/project ast))` with `vm/semantic-contract`; `:stack`/`:register` become `derive/stack-image`/`register-image` over that vector; no other C4 file, no behaviour change, `dht-import-v1.edn` untouched.\nWhat must be true for the owner: the freeze on that one file from the relay of the note until the `srvm-phase8c` merge into `srvm-phase8`; the other seat rebases any uncommitted edit of it afterwards. If the owner refuses the freeze now, 8c stays on its branch unmerged until 8f's freeze; it does not land red.\nGates: the 8c merge gate is the quick tier green including `linked-prelude-test` and `linked-safepoint-test` (27/0) and `bb test:sub:clj yang.python` fast; `dht-import-test` slow stays expected-red in the ledger; Node `bb test:changed` cljs and one Dart lane (`test:changed` cljd plus the transfer peer) on the final tree; 8e may be briefed only after that merge.\n\n## Verdict\nBlocking, scoped: F1 (one line), F2 (one deftest), the harness commit per the ruling. Nothing to revert; the production diff stands as is. Pre-authorized: when `git diff -- src` is byte-identical to the `src/` hunks of `collab/8c-uncommitted.diff`, the test diff adds exactly F1, F2 and the harness port, and the suites above plus the two Python suites are green, the orchestrator may record this report as the Architect sign-off without another round.\nCHANGES_REQUESTED\n;; Criterion 22: one four-way manifest through all four kernels\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(deftest one-four-way-manifest-links-through-all-four-kernels\n  (doseq [policy [:verifying :trusted]]\n    (doseq [format [linker/ast-format linker/semantic-format\n                    linker/stack-format linker/register-format]]\n      (testing (str (name policy) \" \" (name (:format format)))\n        (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n              {:keys [address]} (module-manifest store lt/worked-example)\n              res (link-local store address format (linking format policy))]\n          (is (linker/ok? res))\n          (is (not= :contract-mismatch (:reason res)))\n          (is (= (normalized lt/worked-example)\n                 (b0/normalize (vm/value (run-image format res)))))\n          (jing/close! store))))))\n\n\n(deftest the-manifest-index-resolves-the-images-it-names\n  (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n        {:keys [address]} (module-manifest store lt/worked-example)\n        res (linker/link-manifest\n              (manifest-runtime store {:indexes {}})\n              address :yin.debruijn.code lt/receiver\n              (linking linker/stack-format :verifying))]\n    (is (linker/ok? res))\n    (is (= (lt/stack-image lt/worked-example) (:value res)))\n    (jing/close! store)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Section 8.1: the verifying policy fetches the tree at steps 2 to 4\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- counting-ast-format\n  \"`linker/ast-format` with its whole-value validator and its three\n   scanners counting